<title>DENMARK: Danish Sept/Oct retail sales rise.</title>
<headline>Danish Sept/Oct retail sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's seasonally adjusted retail sales index rose to 108.9 in September and 109.0 in October 1996 from 107.31 in August 1996, the national statistics office said on Monday.  </p>
<p>				  Sept 96   Oct 96     Aug 96</p>
<p>  Season adjusted volume    108.9    109.0     107.3</p>
<p>  Food, beverages,tobacco   103.8    104.1     105.4</p>
<p>  Clothing etc.		 110.1    109.2     106.9</p>
<p>  Other consumer goods	115.6    115.8     110.0</p>
<p>NOTE - 1990 base = 100. The non-seasonally adjusted index for Sept-October 1996 was on average up about 0.3 percent on the same period in 1995, the statistics office said.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
